@page "/sponsor"

<PageTitle>Sponsor BasketElo</PageTitle>

<div class="sponsor-page">
    <section class="sponsor-hero">
        <div class="sponsor-hero-copy">
            <p class="eyebrow">Support independent basketball data</p>
            <h1>Put your brand in front of people who care about the game.</h1>
            <p class="sponsor-lede">
                BasketElo is building a clear, independent way to explore basketball ratings, history, and performance data.
                Sponsorship helps keep the project free while connecting thoughtful brands with a focused audience.
            </p>
            <a class="btn btn-primary sponsor-cta"
               href="https://x.com/sergitm12"
               target="_blank"
               rel="noopener noreferrer">
                Contact @@sergitm12 on X
            </a>
        </div>
        <div class="sponsor-hero-mark" aria-hidden="true">
            <span class="sponsor-mark-ring"></span>
            <span class="sponsor-mark-value">ELO</span>
            <span class="sponsor-mark-caption">basketball intelligence</span>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="sponsor-section sponsor-grid" aria-labelledby="why-sponsor-heading">
        <div>
            <p class="eyebrow">A better kind of ad</p>
            <h2 id="why-sponsor-heading">One beautiful placement, made to belong.</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="sponsor-copy">
            <p>
                The goal is not to fill pages with banners. A sponsor should feel like a useful recommendation:
                relevant to basketball, data, analysis, tools, training, media, or the people who follow the sport.
            </p>
            <p>
                The format will be a single, clearly labelled sponsor placement with a calm visual treatment and a direct link.
                No pop-ups, autoplay, aggressive tracking, or cluttered ad walls.
            </p>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="sponsor-section sponsor-details" aria-labelledby="fit-heading">
        <div class="sponsor-detail-card">
            <span class="sponsor-detail-number">01</span>
            <h2 id="fit-heading">Who it could suit</h2>
            <p>Basketball products, data platforms, coaching tools, sports media, communities, equipment, and thoughtful technology brands.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="sponsor-detail-card">
            <span class="sponsor-detail-number">02</span>
            <h2>What you get</h2>
            <p>A simple, visible association with an independent basketball project and a sponsorship that respects the reader’s attention.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="sponsor-detail-card">
            <span class="sponsor-detail-number">03</span>
            <h2>How it works</h2>
            <p>We discuss fit, agree on a lightweight placement, and review it together. There are no fixed packages yet while the audience is growing.</p>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="sponsor-contact" aria-labelledby="contact-heading">
        <div>
            <p class="eyebrow">Start a conversation</p>
            <h2 id="contact-heading">Have an idea for a good fit?</h2>
            <p>Send a message on X and mention BasketElo sponsorship. Numbers and packages can come later; the first step is finding a useful connection.</p>
        </div>
        <a class="btn btn-outline-primary sponsor-contact-link"
           href="https://x.com/sergitm12"
           target="_blank"
           rel="noopener noreferrer">
            Message @@sergitm12
        </a>
    </section>
</div>
